# Mutation plan for GET /sharedchannels/users/{user_id}/can_dm/{other_user_id} — the two id
# checks, the session, the no-service answer, the service gate, and the legacy config fallback.
#
#   scripts/mutate-batch.sh scripts/mutations/can-dm.plan
#
# Not planned, equivalent on the wire: which of the two ids a 400 names — this server answers the
# untranslated id as its message ([D-092]) and the parameter name lives only in Go's translated
# text, so `second-id-misnamed` and `ids-checked-in-reverse` survived a batch and were dropped.
# Equivalent on the stack:
# view restrictions, so the visibility check never answers false) and the licence half of the
# service gate (the config half is off on both pairs, so the licence side never decides).
#
# Tab-separated: name<TAB>file<TAB>from<TAB>to<TAB>suite<TAB>filter.  `\n` becomes a newline.

